151
00:15:34,450 --> 00:15:40,850
Well, it actually seems that multiple presentation formats, especially if one of

152
00:15:40,850 --> 00:15:44,090
them is visual, help most people learn.

153
00:15:44,090 --> 00:15:50,870
When psychologists and educators test for learning styles, they're trying to figure

154
00:15:50,870 --> 00:15:56,630
out whether these are inherent traits that affect how well students learn, instead

155
00:15:56,630 --> 00:15:58,370
of just a preference.

156
00:15:58,370 --> 00:16:05,270
Usually, they start by giving a survey to figure out what style a student favours,

157
00:16:05,930 --> 00:16:07,990
like visual or verbal learning.

158
00:16:08,470 --> 00:16:15,470
Then they try to the students something with a specific presentation style, like

159
00:16:15,470 --> 00:16:21,170
using visual aids, and do a follow -up test to see how much they learned.

160
00:16:21,170 --> 00:16:27,910
That way, the researchers can see if the self -identified verbal learners really

161
00:16:27,910 --> 00:16:33,150
learned better when the information was just spoken aloud, for example.

162
00:16:33,150 --> 00:16:40,810
But according to a 2008 review, only one study that followed this design found that

163
00:16:40,810 --> 00:16:44,430
students actually learned best with their preferred style.

164
00:16:45,050 --> 00:16:47,330
But the study had some big flaws.

165
00:16:47,330 --> 00:16:52,430
The researchers excluded two -thirds of the original participants because they

166
00:16:52,430 --> 00:16:58,290
didn't seem to have any clear learning style from the survey at the beginning, and

167
00:16:58,290 --> 00:17:02,610
they didn't even report the actual test scores in the final paper.

168
00:17:02,610 --> 00:17:09,610
So, it doesn't really seem like learning styles are an inherent trait that we all

169
00:17:09,610 --> 00:17:15,910
have. But that doesn't mean that all students will do amazingly if they just spend

170
00:17:15,910 --> 00:17:22,570
all their time reading from a Instead, most people seem to learn better if they're

171
00:17:22,570 --> 00:17:26,950
taught in several ways, especially if one is visual.

172
00:17:27,690 --> 00:17:33,170
In one study, researchers tested whether students remembered lists of words better

173
00:17:33,170 --> 00:17:36,530
if they heard them, saw them, or both.

174
00:17:36,530 --> 00:17:43,250
And everyone seemed to do better if they got to see the words in print, even the

175
00:17:43,250 --> 00:17:45,850
self -identified auditory learners.

176
00:17:46,410 --> 00:17:48,530
Their preference didn't seem to matter.

177
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:54,530
Similar studies tested whether students learned basic physics and chemistry concepts

178
00:17:54,530 --> 00:17:59,410
better by reading plain text or viewing pictures, too.

179
00:17:59,410 --> 00:18:01,890
And everyone did better with the help of pictures.

